// REJECTS: Unexpected token
//
// This is the second half of the trap named in ordering-view-modifiers.pure, and the reason
// that one alone is not enough.
//
// On a View the order is   ~filter ~groupBy ~distinct.
// On a class mapping it is ~filter ~distinct ~groupBy.
//
// Same two modifiers, same spelling, opposite order. This file writes the VIEW's order in a
// class mapping; the other file writes the CLASS MAPPING's order in a View. A rewrite that
// shares one modifier routine between the two accepts both files, and a rewrite that hard-
// codes either order and applies it to both rejects one legal construct. Only the pair
// distinguishes a parser that got this right from one that got it uniformly wrong.
###Mapping
Mapping fixture::neg::GroupByBeforeDistinct
(
   fixture::neg::Person: Relational
   {
      ~groupBy
      (
         [fixture::neg::Db]T.ID
      )
      ~distinct
      ~mainTable [fixture::neg::Db]T
      id: [fixture::neg::Db]T.ID
   }
)
